    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d669">

                <pb facs="0790" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg702"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bryan to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-03-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 22, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 70.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that on receipt
                    of your No. 33, of February 26, 1904, announcing the approaching visit to Lisbon
                    of a <pb facs="0791" n="703" xml:id="pg703"/> large American squadron, I
                    communicated the information contained therein to the foreign office.</p>
                <p>The minister for foreign affairs verbally expressed to me the satisfaction that
                    this Government experiences in the prospect of having so many of our finest war
                    ships in Portuguese waters.</p>
                <p>Yesterday, during a function at the Royal Palace, King Carlos heartily announced
                    to me that a cordial welcome awaited our squadron. By many questions he
                    manifested much interest concerning the warships expected and the officers in
                    command of them.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Page
                    Bryan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
